      "content": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstdlib>\n\nstatic const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\nstatic char buf[BUFSIZE];\nstatic int pos = 0, len = 0;\n\ninline char getChar() {\n    if (pos >= len) {\n        len = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n        pos = 0;\n    }\n    return buf[pos++];\n}\n\ninline int readInt() {\n    char c;\n    do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\n    int sign = 1;\n    if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\n    int x = c - '0';\n    for (;;) {\n        c = getChar();\n        if (c < '0' || c > '9') break;\n        x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n    }\n    return sign * x;\n}\n\nstatic inline int maxWindow(const int* __restrict col, int n, int s) {\n    int cur = 0;\n    const int* p = col;\n    for (int i = 0; i < s; ++i) cur += *p++;\n    int mx = cur;\n    const int* add = col + s;\n    const int* sub = col;\n    int j = s;\n    // Unroll by 4 to expose ILP and reduce loop overhead.\n    for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4, add += 4, sub += 4) {\n        cur += add[0] - sub[0];\n        if (cur > mx) mx = cur;\n        cur += add[1] - sub[1];\n        if (cur > mx) mx = cur;\n        cur += add[2] - sub[2];\n        if (cur > mx) mx = cur;\n        cur += add[3] - sub[3];\n        if (cur > mx) mx = cur;\n    }\n    for (; j < n; ++j, ++add, ++sub) {\n        cur += *add - *sub;\n        if (cur > mx) mx = cur;\n    }\n    return mx;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = readInt();\n    int s = readInt();\n\n    // Cache-line aligned allocations for better vectorization and fewer conflicts.\n    void* colMem = nullptr;\n    void* rowsMem = nullptr;\n    if (posix_memalign(&colMem, 64, sizeof(int) * n) != 0) return 1;\n    if (posix_memalign(&rowsMem, 64, sizeof(int) * (size_t)s * n) != 0) {\n        free(colMem);\n        return 1;\n    }\n    int* colSum = static_cast<int*>(colMem);\n    int* rows = static_cast<int*>(rowsMem);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) colSum[i] = 0;\n\n    // Initial S rows: fill ring buffer and column sums.\n    for (int r = 0; r < s; ++r) {\n        int* row = rows + (size_t)r * n;\n        int c = 0;\n        for (; c + 3 < n; c += 4) {\n            int v0 = readInt(), v1 = readInt(), v2 = readInt(), v3 = readInt();\n            row[c] = v0; colSum[c] += v0;\n            row[c+1] = v1; colSum[c+1] += v1;\n            row[c+2] = v2; colSum[c+2] += v2;\n            row[c+3] = v3; colSum[c+3] += v3;\n        }\n        for (; c < n; ++c) {\n            int v = readInt();\n            row[c] = v;\n            colSum[c] += v;\n        }\n    }\n\n    int mx = maxWindow(colSum, n, s);\n\n    // Slide the vertical window one row at a time.\n    for (int r = s; r < n; ++r) {\n        int ringPos = r % s;\n        int* row = rows + (size_t)ringPos * n;\n        int c = 0;\n        // Unrolled update: read old values, new values, and update colSum.\n        for (; c + 3 < n; c += 4) {\n            int old0 = row[c], old1 = row[c+1], old2 = row[c+2], old3 = row[c+3];\n            int v0 = readInt(), v1 = readInt(), v2 = readInt(), v3 = readInt();\n            row[c] = v0; colSum[c] += v0 - old0;\n            row[c+1] = v1; colSum[c+1] += v1 - old1;\n            row[c+2] = v2; colSum[c+2] += v2 - old2;\n            row[c+3] = v3; colSum[c+3] += v3 - old3;\n        }\n        for (; c < n; ++c) {\n            int old = row[c];\n            int v = readInt();\n            row[c] = v;\n            colSum[c] += v - old;\n        }\n        int curMax = maxWindow(colSum, n, s);\n        if (curMax > mx) mx = curMax;\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", mx);\n\n    free(rowsMem);\n    free(colMem);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Aligning the column-sum and ring-buffer arrays to cache lines, adding restrict qualifiers, and unrolling the inner update/maximum loops by four improves memory locality and instruction-level parallelism on ARM64 without changing the streaming algorithm.",
  "notes": "The algorithm remains identical: a ring buffer of S rows with incremental vertical sums and a horizontal sliding-window scan. Only micro-optimizations were applied (aligned allocations, __restrict, 4x unrolling). Correctness is preserved for all valid inputs; no benchmark-specific specialization was introduced.",
